config BR2_PACKAGE_MUIR
	bool "muir"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	help
	  muir itself, on the board's own Arm cores, beside the CADR in
	  the fabric.  It is built from muir's own source at the commit
	  muir.commit pins, so the board runs the muir this repository is
	  held to.  No binary is carried in this repository.

	  It is here to be the debugger.  MIT debugged a CADR with a
	  second CADR over the debug cable, running CC.  This fabric has
	  the debuggee end of that cable, and muir on the Arm cores is
	  the machine at the other end of it.  It reaches the fabric
	  through a register window over /dev/mem rather than over a
	  wire.

	  Every other program in this tree has an init script and this
	  one has none.  muir is started by hand when it is wanted.  The
	  reason is the cable and not the cost: a debugger that dies
	  mid-request leaves the debuggee's own bus cycle waiting.
	  Running muir costs the fabric CADR nothing, measured with both
	  cores saturated and the machine's rate read off the fabric's
	  own tick counter.

	  /root/.muirrc is a symlink to muirrc on the pack partition, so
	  that the debugger is the word `muir` and its settings survive a
	  reboot.  The root filesystem is a RAM disk unpacked at every
	  boot, so an edit made to a file in it is lost.

comment "muir needs a toolchain the Rust compiler supports"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
